  "finding": "Default first touch placed all buffers on node 1 in low-bandwidth runs. Explicit per-worker local binding split pages evenly and restored the high-bandwidth regime. Subsequent default allocations also split evenly after local memory was reclaimed.",
  "limits": [
    "Earlier 34/83 GB/s runs did not record placement, so the exact historical cause is inferred, not directly observed.",
    "Page counts aggregate buffer-containing mappings; not per-thread memory-controller traffic.",
    "Measured read bandwidth is not theoretical DRAM bandwidth or quantized-kernel utilization.",
    "Strict binding can induce reclaim; allocation and reclaim are outside the scan timer."
  ],
